Schema/types drift check (TASK-026)

Add an automated check that verifies packages/shared/src/types.ts (the hand-written type contract shared by apps/web and apps/mobile) stays in sync with the actual database schema defined in supabase/migrations/**. Wire it up as `npm run check:types`. Per the 2026-08-29 spec amendment, use a static migration-parsing design (parse the migration files directly) rather than depending on a live/local Supabase instance, dropping the earlier local-Supabase dependency. The check should fail if a migration adds, drops, or renames a column that isn't reflected in types.ts. Schema and types are currently in sync, so this run establishes the passing baseline.
